    <!-- Privacy note (PLAN §7). Same text as docs/privacy.md: keep the two in sync. -->
    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy note</string>
    <string name="privacy_intro">RW Radar collects as little as it can. Here is what that means.</string>
    <string name="privacy_collected_title">What we collect</string>
    <string name="privacy_collected">• An anonymous ID that Firebase creates when you first open the app. It is not linked to your name or account.\n• The companies you follow and the role families you pick (for example Engineering or Data).\n• Your notification settings.\n• Usage events (for example \"followed a company\" or \"opened a notification\") and crash reports, so we can fix bugs.</string>
    <string name="privacy_not_collected_title">What we don\'t collect</string>
    <string name="privacy_not_collected">Your name, email address, phone number, contacts, location or résumé.</string>
    <string name="privacy_storage_title">Where it\'s stored</string>
    <string name="privacy_storage">In Google Firebase (Firestore, Analytics and Crashlytics).</string>
    <string name="privacy_delete_title">How to delete it</string>
    <string name="privacy_delete">• Uninstalling the app (or clearing its data) removes the anonymous ID from your phone. Your follows can\'t be recovered after that.\n• To delete the data stored on the server for your ID, email somshekharpandey@gmail.com and we will remove it.</string>
    <string name="privacy_links_title">News and job links</string>
    <string name="privacy_links">• News headlines link to the publisher\'s own website. Job links open the company\'s own job posting. RW Radar doesn\'t store article text.\n• The \"Get referred on ReferralWorld\" button opens the ReferralWorld Careers website. RW Radar doesn\'t share any data with ReferralWorld.</string>
</resources>
